# Cloudflare Pages response headers
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# The two __..._HASHES__ tokens in the Content-Security-Policy line are replaced after every build by
# scripts/csp.mjs, which hashes each inline <script> and <style> that Astro writes into dist/.
# Always build with `npm run build` (not `astro build` alone) before deploying.
# Limits: 100 rules, 2,000 characters per line (the build step checks the second).

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; script-src 'self' __SCRIPT_HASHES__; style-src 'self' __STYLE_HASHES__; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Build output is fingerprinted, so it can be cached for a year
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
